# mcp-mrtr-elicit-declined - a declined prompt is terminal: the tool reports the
# refusal and the server does not ask again.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-mcp2026-2-mrtr AC-8 and end-to-end user story 2. The client
# declares form mode, is prompted, and answers {"action":"decline"} on the
# retry. That is an ANSWER, not an omission, so the handler completes with an
# error naming the outcome instead of returning a second InputRequiredResult.
#
# WHAT CHANGED AND WHY: this replaces elicitation-decline.ci, whose decline
# travelled as a client JSON-RPC response correlated to a server-initiated
# request -- a message the 2026-07-28 transport forbids the client to send.
# The distinction being proved is the same one and is now load-bearing for a
# different reason: under MRTR a server MAY prompt repeatedly, so if a decline
# were treated as "the client did not answer", a user who has explicitly said no
# would be asked forever.
#
# PREVENTS: a decline collapsing into the re-ask path (an unbounded prompt loop
# driven by a refusing client), and a decline being dispatched as an empty
# command.

stdin=mcp:terminator=EOF_MCP
elicit-answer decline
@ze_execute {}
EOF_MCP

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 1
				remote 1
			}
			router-id 1.2.3.4
			family {
				ipv4/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
			}
			capability {
				graceful-restart disable
			}
		}
		behavior {
			group-updates disable
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze --mcp $PORT -:stdin=ze-bgp
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze-test mcp --port $PORT --elicit form:stdin=mcp:timeout=20s
# ze-test mcp prints the tool error to stderr and exits non-zero.
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stderr:contains=declined
expect=stderr:contains=command error
# One round trip only. The client bounds itself at maxInputRounds and reports
# "still required input after N attempts" if the server kept prompting; seeing
# the decline text instead is what proves the loop terminated on the answer.
reject=stderr:pattern=still required input
